{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "Initiates the process and captures the initial return action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n2",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the XOR decision for return method and captures the customer return path. Condition modeled as action/guard preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n3",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the crew pickup path and converges the two return methods. Structural plumbing and condition-to-action retyping preserve behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the counting and comparison step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the order status decision and captures the complete order path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the incomplete order path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the damaged items path. Core decision logic and flow are preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the disposition decision and captures the packing for existing order path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the storing for future orders path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for notifying the customer about missing items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for temporarily removing damaged items from inventory."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b4->n11",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the missing item resolution decision and captures the return path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b4->n12",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the non-return path for missing items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly marks the first process termination point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b5->n14",
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the repair decision and captures the successful repair path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b5->n15",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the discard path and joins the repair outcomes. Structural convergence preserves flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n16",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order. If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the final disposition decision and captures the second packing path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n17",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the second storing path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The customer is then emailed with replacement charges, and the process is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Marks the final process termination after the concluding notification."
    }
  ],
